        "explanation": "Blanche married Allan at sixteen, discovered his homosexuality, told him he disgusted her, and he shot himself that same night while the Varsouviana played. Desire, guilt, and death fused in one moment, so that ever after love and dying are inseparable for her. Her later promiscuity chases the light that died with Allan; the rest of the play is that night's long echo.",
